{
 "summary": "Gateway began returning 500s on POST /checkout and GET /products shortly after gateway was deployed 1.4.2 -> 1.5.1 at 07:40:21Z. From 07:40:24Z it logged 'route table not loaded' 87 times, and its 5xx ratio crossed 5% at 07:40:51Z (avg 14.7%, max 34.7%). The failing traces end at gateway within 1-14ms, and downstream inventory and orders show no errors. The most likely cause is the gateway 1.5.1 release failing to load its route table; rolling back to 1.4.2 is the primary mitigation.",
 "root_cause": {
  "statement": "Gateway release 1.5.1 fails to load its route table, so gateway rejects some requests with 500 locally without calling downstream services. The deploy is linked to the failures in several ways: the 'route table not loaded' errors start 3s after the deploy, and every failing trace and log entry is tagged release 1.5.1. The failing traces contain only a gateway span and finish in milliseconds, which fits a local failure rather than a timeout cascade.",
  "service": "gateway",
  "confidence": "high",
  "evidence_ids": [
   "ev-965d5c78fedd",
   "ev-a2ab9bd2abea",
   "ev-7c8fa7ec0430",
